   "source": [
    "A fitted distribution is a model, not a guarantee that the observations actually follow it. Use a graphical goodness-of-fit check to compare each fitted distribution with the empirical distribution. Inspect the agreement across the observed range, paying particular attention to regions where the curves diverge. No formal hypothesis test is required here.\n"
